  "question": {
    "text": "If a variable line&nbsp;<math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is such that the two circles <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>78</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> are on its opposite sides, then the set of all values of <math><mi>&#955;</mi></math> is the interval :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mn>23</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>23</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>31</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>21</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>17</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
